course: dictionary
lesson: 15770
title: Tudor, a word with a history
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a time in history, and «Tudor» is one of them. When it has a capital letter, it often means the Tudors, the family of kings and queens who ruled England. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning is used.
explain: «The Tudors ruled England from 1485 to 1603.» Here Tudors names a royal family, so it is a noun. «Tudor houses have black beams and white walls.» Here Tudor is an adjective: it tells you the houses belong to that time or style.
explain: The topic gives clues too. If a text talks about Henry VIII, the Armada or Shakespeare, it is about Tudor times. Ask yourself: is this word naming people, describing a time or style, or naming a building? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: The Tudors were the family who ruled England from 1485 to 1603.
fact: Famous Tudor rulers include Henry VII, Henry VIII, Edward VI, Mary I and Elizabeth I.
fact: «Tudor» can describe things from that time, such as «Tudor clothes».
fact: A Tudor house has black wooden beams and white walls. Some modern houses copy this style, which is called mock Tudor.
fact: Henry VIII had six wives, and Tudor history is a big topic in UK history lessons.
exercise: Which of these people was a Tudor ruler? | Queen Victoria | Winston Churchill | Isaac Newton | *Henry VIII
exercise: «The old Tudor house had black beams and white walls.» What does Tudor describe? | A modern shop | Something very new | *Belonging to the Tudor time or style
exercise: «Henry VIII was one of the Tudors.» Which word names a royal family? | was | one | *Tudors | Henry
test: Which dates show when the Tudors ruled England? | *1485 to 1603 | 1914 to 1918 | 1837 to 1901 | 1066 to 1154
test: A house with black wooden beams and white walls is in which style? | Georgian | Victorian | *Tudor | Roman
exam: Which sentence uses Tudor as a noun, naming a royal family? | *«The Tudors ruled England from 1485 to 1603.» | «Tudor houses have white walls.» | «Tudor clothes were on show.»
